# Copy to .github-runner.env (gitignored) and fill in a real token to let
# 04-setup-ci-runner.sh deploy self-registering GitHub Actions runners.
# Either value can also be passed as an environment variable of the same
# name, which takes precedence over this file.
#
# GITHUB_RUNNER_PAT: a fine-grained token (GitHub -> Settings -> Developer
# settings -> Personal access tokens -> Fine-grained tokens), with:
#   - Resource owner: the account or org that owns GITHUB_REPO
#   - Repository access: "Only select repositories" -> GITHUB_REPO only
#   - Repository permissions:
#       Administration: Read and write  (register/deregister/list runners)
#       Metadata: Read-only             (added automatically)
#     everything else: No access
# Administration: write also allows changing the repo's settings, so keep
# the token scoped to this one repo. A classic token would need the whole
# "repo" scope (every repo you can access) - avoid it.
#
# Runners re-register with this token after every job, so CI stops once it
# expires: pick an expiry that outlasts the project, or rotate it by
# updating this file and re-running ./04-setup-ci-runner.sh.
GITHUB_RUNNER_PAT="github_pat_..."
# owner/name; defaults to the repo behind this checkout's 'origin' remote.
GITHUB_REPO="sammosios/dd2482-project"
